# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored and must never be committed.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# Everything that reads credentials (npm run verify:provider, npm start,
# npm run dev) loads .env automatically via Node's --env-file-if-exists,
# so there is nothing to export and nothing to remember per shell.
#
# On the Pi these do NOT live here — they go in /etc/mirrormirror/server.env
# (root-owned, mode 0600), outside the repo entirely. See ops/README.md.

# Cloudflare Workers AI. Create a scoped token at
# https://dash.cloudflare.com/profile/api-tokens with only:
#   Account · Workers AI · Read      (nothing else, and never the Global API Key)
# Give it an expiry a little past the show, and note the token ID so it can be
# rolled if the Pi walks off — it is a physical device in a public room.
CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=
CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=

# Optional overrides.
# GENERATION_MODEL=@cf/moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code
# GENERATION_MODEL=@cf/moonshotai/kimi-k2.6      # general vision variant, worth A/B-ing
# GENERATION_TIMEOUT_MS=5500
# GENERATION_MAX_TOKENS=1200

# Comparison path only.
# GENERATION_PROVIDER=openai
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
